# Source is always text: a stray NUL byte otherwise makes a file "binary" to
# git, which silently drops it out of diffs and `--numstat` (reported as -\t-),
# so a change lands where review cannot see it. `scripts/no-raw-nul-bytes.test.ts`
# in the parent repo keeps the bytes clean; this keeps the diffs readable either
# way, including across the commit that removes one.
*.ts   text diff
*.tsx  text diff
*.js   text diff
*.mjs  text diff
*.json text diff
